@startuml Inventory_Domain_Model

title Inventory Management System - Domain Model

hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class BusinessPartner {
  +partnerCode: int
  +name: text
  +address: text
}

class Vendor <<role>>
class Buyer <<role>>

class Unit {
  +id: int
  +unitName: text
}

class Item {
  +itemCode: int
  +description: text
  +quantity: real
}

abstract class Invoice {
  +invoiceNo: int
  +date: date
  +quantity: real
  +ratePerUnit: real
  +amountPaid: real
}

class PurchaseInvoice
class SalesInvoice

Vendor --|> BusinessPartner
Buyer --|> BusinessPartner

Invoice <|-- PurchaseInvoice
Invoice <|-- SalesInvoice

Unit "1" <-- "0..*" Item : measured in

Item "1" <-- "0..*" PurchaseInvoice : purchased item
Item "1" <-- "0..*" SalesInvoice : sold item

Vendor "1" <-- "0..*" PurchaseInvoice : supplier
Buyer "1" <-- "0..*" SalesInvoice : customer

note right of BusinessPartner
Implemented in the database as table: vendors.

The application reuses the same table
for both vendors and buyers/customers.
end note

note right of Item
Implemented in the database as table: items.

Item.quantity represents the current stock.
end note

note bottom of PurchaseInvoice
A purchase increases the stock quantity
of the selected item.
end note

note bottom of SalesInvoice
A sale decreases the stock quantity
of the selected item.

Sale quantity must not exceed available stock.
end note

note bottom of Invoice
Invoice amount is based on:

quantity * ratePerUnit
end note

@enduml
